"""Create an executable research notebook using project modules, not copied reference code."""
import nbformat as nbf
from pathlib import Path
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
n=nbf.v4.new_notebook()
n.metadata={'kernelspec':{'display_name':'Python 3 (PhishGuard environment)','language':'python','name':'python3'}}
cells=[
('m','# PhishGuard AI — phishing detection research\n\nQuestion: How accurately can machine-learning models distinguish phishing from legitimate websites using URL-based features? The exact reference input is akashkr/phishing-website-dataset, version 2. Labels are verified in the source data card: −1 phishing, +1 legitimate. The data contain encoded features, not raw URLs. This notebook does not visit websites.'),
('c',"from pathlib import Path\nimport sys, json\nroot = Path.cwd()\nif root.name == 'notebooks': root = root.parent\nsys.path.insert(0, str(root / 'src'))\nfrom preprocess import load_data, LEXICAL\nraw, clean, features, sha256 = load_data()\nprint('Shape:', raw.shape, 'SHA-256:', sha256)\nprint(raw['Result'].value_counts())\nraw.head()"),
('m','## Data exploration and provenance\nThe index is an identifier and never a predictor. Missing values and duplicates are measured before preprocessing. Source definitions are summarized in docs/feature-descriptions.json. Features such as certificate trust, page anchors, DNS and traffic require external observations.'),
('c',"print('Missing cells:', int(raw.isna().sum().sum()))\nprint('Exact duplicate rows:', int(raw.duplicated().sum()))\nprint('Duplicates excluding identifier:', len(raw)-len(clean))\nprint('Retained:', len(clean))\nraw[features].describe().T"),
('m','## Methods fixed before evaluation\nDeduplicate identical feature-and-label rows, preserving contradictory labels. Group identical predictor patterns within each feature set. Use the first shuffled StratifiedGroupKFold split (5 folds, seed 42), giving approximately 80/20 train/test. Fit imputation and one-hot encoding inside each training pipeline. Encoded states are categorical; scaling arbitrary −1/0/+1 distances is not appropriate here. One-hot values are already on a common 0/1 scale. Apply balanced class weights only if the training class ratio exceeds 1.5. No test-driven hyperparameter tuning. Compare Logistic Regression (C=1) and Random Forest (250 trees, minimum leaf size 2).'),
('c',"from train import run\nresults = run()\nimport pandas as pd\nrows=[]\nfor scope, exp in results['experiments'].items():\n    print(scope, {k:v for k,v in exp['split'].items() if not k.endswith('source_ids')})\n    for name, m in exp['models'].items():\n        rows.append({'scope':scope,'model':name,**{k:m[k] for k in ['accuracy','precision','recall','f1','roc_auc']}})\npd.DataFrame(rows)"),
('m','## Measured charts\nRaw distributions describe the source; correlation uses deduplicated encoded predictors. ROC and confusion matrices use held-out predictions with phishing as positive. Separate feature-set splits prevent shared feature patterns, but do not make the scopes a paired experiment.'),
('c',"from IPython.display import display, Image\nfor name in ['classes','feature-distributions','missing','correlation','url-comparison','url-confusion','url-roc','url-importance','full-comparison','full-confusion','full-roc','full-importance']:\n    display(Image(filename=str(root/'results'/'charts'/(name+'.png'))))"),
('m','## Error inspection\nFalse negatives miss phishing; false positives block legitimate records. Uncalibrated model probabilities are not confidence guarantees. Browse held-out mistakes without selecting them for training.'),
('c',"errors = [r for r in results['experiments']['url']['records'] if any(p['label'] != r['actual'] for p in r['predictions'].values())]\nprint('URL-scope records misclassified by at least one model:',len(errors))\nerrors[:3]"),
('m','## Limitations and reproducibility\nThis historical snapshot lacks URLs, timestamps and domain groups. Pattern grouping addresses exact duplicates, not related-domain or temporal leakage. Categorical feature definitions include older reputation signals and incomplete extraction rules. A single holdout gives no confidence interval. Do not deploy this as a live safety checker. See docs/report.md for interpretation and references. Run src/export_site.py after the analysis to embed current results in the existing HTML.'),
('c',"assert all(e['split']['group_overlap']==0 for e in results['experiments'].values())\nassert all(sum(map(sum,m['confusion']))==e['split']['test'] for e in results['experiments'].values() for m in e['models'].values())\nprint('Verified: no shared predictor groups; confusion totals match test sizes.')")]
n.cells=[nbf.v4.new_markdown_cell(s) if t=='m' else nbf.v4.new_code_cell(s) for t,s in cells]
nbf.write(n,ROOT/'notebooks/phishing_analysis.ipynb')
